# .gitignore of the reproduction package
#
# Policy: no data enter the repository by accident. Every data, figure, archive and binary file
# type is ignored everywhere, whatever folder it sits in. A file of such a type is tracked only
# through an explicit re-include in the last section ("Deliberate exceptions"): one entry per file
# or folder, with a comment saying why the package needs it. Do not use `git add -f` to get around
# this file; a forced add leaves no record of the decision.
#
# The rules exclude by file type, not by folder (except for the generated-output folders in
# section 3), so that a re-include below can take effect: git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent folder is excluded.
#
# Before every commit, check what git would add:
#   git status --short --untracked-files=all
#   git status --short --ignored --untracked-files=all    (what is held back, and why: git check-ignore -v <path>)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Anonymity: files that name the authors, the group or their machines (until camera-ready)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# local agent notes
/CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/
# slides with the author's name
/experiments/decoder_timing/hw/presentation/
# environment records with the host name (user name and group)
/experiments/network/env/ENVIRONMENT.md
/experiments/decoder_timing/hw/env/ENVIRONMENT.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Secrets and credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.Renviron
.netrc
.qiskit/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.token
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Generated outputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build folders at any depth (11 Nov 2026): each analysis folder writes into its own build/
# (analysis/*/build/); also the repository-level build/ of the template and the compiled drivers of
# the experiments
build/
# figure folders of the experiment scripts' own plots (experiments/*/figures/), at any depth
figures/
# Rust build output of the fusion-blossom timing driver
target/
# all experiment data: data/ holds the recorded campaign (data/zenodo/, archived on Zenodo) and the literature
# tables (data/literature/); the experiments and the analysis get its path as a setting (data/README.md). Only
# data/literature/, the README files and the checksum list are tracked (re-included in section 10).
/data/**

