# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. Deliberate exceptions
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-include data here, one entry per file or folder, each with a comment saying why the package
# needs it and where it comes from. Example (do not uncomment without deciding it):
#   # reference statistics compared by `make check` (step 5); copied from experiments/rtas/trip_time/stats
#   !/reproduction/data/reference/*.csv
#
# Tool metadata of an otherwise ignored type (not data):
# renv's project settings, tracked together with renv.lock if the environment is pinned with renv
!/renv/settings.json
# Python dependency lists of the experiments (their .venv folders are not copied; rebuild from these)
!requirements*.txt
# CMake build descriptions of the C++ timing drivers (source code, not data)
!/experiments/decoder_timing/drivers/*/CMakeLists.txt
# vendored third-party input: the noiseless bivariate-bicycle memory circuits from the tesseract-decoder test
# data (68 kB, commit in vendor/VENDOR.md); the BB syndromes are generated from them
!/experiments/decoder_timing/vendor/tesseract_circuits/*.noiseless.stim
# GPU state during the hardware experiment's GPU runs (driver, CUDA, clocks, decoder versions; written by
# `make gpu`, cited by experiments/decoder_timing/hw/README.md); an environment record, no names
!/experiments/decoder_timing/hw/env/gpu_env.txt
# data/: the folders (so that git looks inside), the README files and the checksum list; these describe
# and verify the data, they are not data themselves
!/data/**/
!/data/**/README.md
!/data/SHA256SUMS
# data/literature/: the sourced constants and third-party data the experiments read (no experiment produces them),
# each value with its source
!/data/literature/**
#
# Data: (none yet)
